{"author":{"id":"2462ded6f56967dde059994c39a506c79e39e5dfd10c5a07f07a23a5652a8353"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1776199185,"nonce":"ivfzugvcxD0c1OM2v7aPSizIc0s=","title":"Watcher tries to relaunch coder instead of review after completion","message":"## Problem\n\nAfter a coder session completes and reaches `waiting:review`, the watcher repeatedly tries to relaunch the coder session instead of launching a review session. This causes a loop of \"session already exists\" errors:\n\n```\nError: session already exists for issue 8dc9864e19ffd348ae74de79633562a95467128f16c96b0b6c0450a48497894c\nCreated worktree at /home/akhavr/src/agent-worker/.worktrees/agent-8dc9864e19ff\nDumped issue + 0 issues to /home/akhavr/src/agent-worker/.nightshift/sessions/8dc9864e19ff\nLaunching container nightshift-8dc9864e19ff...\nError: session already exists for issue ...\nError: session already exists for issue ...\n```\n\nThe watcher should detect that a coder session exists in `waiting:review` status and launch a review session (`review-\u003cid\u003e`) instead of trying to relaunch the coder.\n\n## Root cause investigation\n\nCheck `host/watcher/review_orchestrator.py` and `host/watcher/session_monitor.py` for the logic that decides when to launch a review vs when to (incorrectly) try relaunching the coder.\n\nThe issue may be in `find_existing_session_by_prefix()` in `host/launch.py` — it finds the coder session and blocks the launch, but doesn't distinguish between \"launch coder\" and \"launch review\" cases.\n\n## Tests (write first, must fail before implementation)\n- tests/watcher/test_review_orchestrator.py::test_launches_review_not_coder_after_completion\n  Assert: when coder session is in `waiting:review`, watcher calls launch with `--step review`, not coder\n- tests/test_launch.py::test_find_existing_session_allows_review_when_coder_exists\n  Assert: `find_existing_session_by_prefix()` does not block review launch when coder session exists\n\n## Files\n- host/watcher/review_orchestrator.py (investigate)\n- host/launch.py (likely fix in find_existing_session_by_prefix)\n- tests/watcher/test_review_orchestrator.py (add test)\n- tests/test_launch.py (add test)\n\n## Implementation\n1. Investigate the session detection logic in launch.py\n2. Modify `find_existing_session_by_prefix()` to allow review sessions when coder exists\n3. Or fix the watcher to pass correct flags that bypass the check for review launches\n\nREQ: REQ-031","files":null}]}